<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct beef imports slip by 14.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct beef imports slip by 14.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in October totalled 45,078 tonnes, down by 14.0 percent from the same period a year earlier, according to data released by the Finance Ministry on Thursday. Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Oct 96	 Sept 96    Oct 95</p>
<p> Total	    45,078	 34,542     52,405</p>
<p> Refrigerated   27,257	 20,530     29,629</p>
<p> Frozen	   17,821	 14,012     22,776</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     16,068	 11,437     16,895</p>
<p>  U.S.	    10,598	  8,533     12,050</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Oct 96	Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> U.S.	     11,075	 8,048	13,268</p>
<p> Australia	 5,062	 4,757	 6,675</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first 10 months of 1996 were 267,839 tonnes against 297,005 tonnes during the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the first 10 months of 1996 came to 271,334 tonnes against 234,933 tonnes in the same period of 1995.</p>
</text>
